The formed bowl has exactly three direct consumers: basket shaping, jar shaping and firing. The mandatory earlier basket and jar exist before the earned kiln action; the existing event-local transformation can therefore replace the actual unfired bowl at firing without a new cleanup rule. The optional brine route requires deliberate relocation of the actual fired bowl from its earlier location; it does not silently import extra inventory.

